## Experiment 1: Union-Find Operations

**Q1. What is Union-Find?**

Ans: A data structure used to maintain and merge disjoint sets.

**Q2. What is DSU?**

Ans: Disjoint Set Union.

**Q3. What are disjoint sets?**

Ans: Sets that do not contain any common elements.

**Q4. What are the basic operations of Union-Find?**

Ans: Make Set, Find and Union.

**Q5. What is the Find operation?**

Ans: It identifies the representative or root of a set.

**Q6. What is the Union operation?**

Ans: It combines two different sets into a single set.

**Q7. What is path compression?**

Ans: An optimization technique that directly connects visited nodes to their root during the Find operation.

**Q8. What is union by rank?**

Ans: An optimization technique that attaches the tree with smaller rank to the tree with larger rank.

**Q9. What is the initial parent of each element?**

Ans: The element itself.

**Q10. What is the initial rank of each element?**

Ans: Zero.

**Q11. How do we check whether two people belong to the same group?**

Ans: By checking whether both people have the same root representative.

**Q12. What is the time complexity of optimized Union-Find?**

Ans: O(alpha(n)) amortized per Union or Find operation.

**Q13. What is the space complexity of Union-Find?**

Ans: O(n).

**Q14. What is the inverse Ackermann function?**

Ans: An extremely slowly growing mathematical function used in the complexity analysis of Union-Find.

**Q15. What are the applications of Union-Find?**

Ans: Social networks, connected components, network connectivity, cycle detection and Kruskal's algorithm.

**Q16. Can Union-Find detect cycles?**

Ans: Yes, in undirected graphs.

**Q17. What happens when two elements already belong to the same set?**

Ans: The Union operation does not modify the sets.

**Q18. Why is Union-Find useful in social networks?**

Ans: It efficiently identifies people belonging to the same connected social group.

**Q19. What is a connected component?**

Ans: A maximal group of vertices connected through paths in an undirected graph.

**Q20. Can standard Union-Find efficiently delete friendship connections?**

Ans: No. Standard Union-Find supports merging sets but does not efficiently support splitting them.
